{"units": [{"id": "en-quote215", "translation": "Pray for such things to the gods without lamentation, and not in vain and wild snortings."}, {"id": "en-quote216", "translation": "The work of war will be decided by the dice."}, {"id": "en-quote217", "translation": "And he too shouts in the syllables of letters."}, {"id": "en-quote218", "translation": "To honor with reverence."}, {"id": "en-quote219", "translation": "In one blow great prosperity has been destroyed."}, {"id": "en-quote220", "translation": "For you will hear the whole story, Darius, in a brief account."}, {"id": "en-quote221", "translation": "To speak of those who were killed in the vote."}, {"id": "en-quote222", "translation": "And with two laments he released his limbs."}, {"id": "en-quote223", "translation": "In hostile funerals you dared to bury a man without lamentation."}, {"id": "en-quote224", "translation": "To hate another bloody Scylla in words (Weil reads στυγῶ)."}, {"id": "en-quote225", "translation": "For I learn by report."}, {"id": "en-quote226", "translation": "Alas, again in the third address."}, {"id": "en-quote227", "translation": "These gods I invoke in prayers as a prelude. And Pallas Pronaia is honored in words."}, {"id": "en-quote228", "translation": "She once found a memory that repaid in prayers."}, {"id": "en-quote229", "translation": "He did not resolve the quarrel by taking silver."}, {"id": "en-quote230", "translation": "And the fiery sun, shining upon the earth, melts the rocky snow."}, {"id": "en-word1", "translation": "in the house"}, {"id": "en-word2", "translation": "in the halls"}, {"id": "en-word3", "translation": "at the gates"}, {"id": "en-word4", "translation": "in the gateways 799. in the land"}, {"id": "en-word5", "translation": "earth"}, {"id": "en-word6", "translation": "in the ground"}, {"id": "en-word7", "translation": "in the city"}, {"id": "en-word8", "translation": "in places"}, {"id": "en-word9", "translation": "in the hands"}, {"id": "en-word10", "translation": "in the hands"}, {"id": "en-word11", "translation": "in the mind"}, {"id": "en-word12", "translation": "in the mind"}, {"id": "en-word13", "translation": "in troubles"}, {"id": "en-word14", "translation": "in Hades"}, {"id": "en-word15", "translation": "house"}, {"id": "en-word16", "translation": "into"}, {"id": "en-word17", "translation": "in"}, {"id": "en-word18", "translation": "in"}, {"id": "en-word19", "translation": "among mortals"}, {"id": "en-word20", "translation": "in"}, {"id": "en-word21", "translation": "as the speech proceeds"}, {"id": "en-word22", "translation": "in"}, {"id": "en-word23", "translation": "in"}, {"id": "en-word24", "translation": "in"}, {"id": "en-word25", "translation": "in"}, {"id": "en-word26", "translation": "but"}, {"id": "en-word27", "translation": "and in"}, {"id": "en-word28", "translation": "in which the fiery sun"}, {"id": "en-word29", "translation": "in"}, {"id": "en-word30", "translation": "the, the (acc.)"}, {"id": "en-word31", "translation": "and, and in"}, {"id": "enages-orth1", "translation": "accursed, under a curse"}, {"id": "enages-def1", "translation": "accursed"}, {"id": "enages-note1", "translation": "Explained by the scholiast through ἐναγίσματα [offerings to the dead]."}, {"id": "enages-quote1", "translation": "And to the gods accursed offerings."}, {"id": "enages-word1", "translation": "offerings to the dead"}, {"id": "enagonios-orth1", "translation": "presiding over games"}, {"id": "enagonios-def1", "translation": "presiding over games"}, {"id": "enagonios-quote1", "translation": "O Hermes, who presides over games, son of Maia and Zeus."}, {"id": "enairo-orth1", "translation": "to kill"}, {"id": "enairo-def1", "translation": "to kill"}, {"id": "enairo-quote1", "translation": "Thus they were killed too much by their sisters' hands."}, {"id": "enaisimos-orth1", "translation": "befitting one's lot, just"}, {"id": "enaisimos-def1", "translation": "befitting one's lot, just"}, {"id": "enaisimos-quote1", "translation": "Honor the life that is befitting."}, {"id": "enaisimos_adv-orth1", "translation": "fittingly"}, {"id": "enaisimos_adv-def1", "translation": "fittingly"}, {"id": "enaisimos_adv-quote1", "translation": "To praise fittingly."}, {"id": "enaisios-orth1", "translation": "fitting"}, {"id": "enaisios-def1", "translation": "fitting"}, {"id": "enaisios-quote1", "translation": "He committed no less outrages, not fitting for me."}, {"id": "enalios-orth1", "translation": "of the sea"}, {"id": "enalios-def1", "translation": "of the sea"}, {"id": "enalios-quote1", "translation": "May they save their friends from the paths of the sea."}, {"id": "enallomai-orth1", "translation": "to leap upon"}, {"id": "enallomai-def1", "translation": "to leap upon"}, {"id": "enallomai-note1", "translation": "Elmsley rightly reads ἐνήλω [leapt upon], as we said under the word ἅλλομαι p. 19 b."}, {"id": "enallomai-quote1", "translation": "How heavily you leapt with your feet upon the whole Persian race."}, {"id": "enallomai-word1", "translation": "leapt upon"}, {"id": "enallomai-word2", "translation": "see ἅλλομαι"}, {"id": "enantioomai-orth1", "translation": "to oppose"}, {"id": "enantioomai-def1", "translation": "to oppose"}, {"id": "enantioomai-quote1", "translation": "I will not oppose not to proclaim all that you need."}, {"id": "enantios-orth1", "translation": "opposite, contrary"}, {"id": "enantios-def1", "translation": "opposite, contrary"}, {"id": "enantios-def2", "translation": "adversary, enemy"}, {"id": "enantios-quote1", "translation": "And to the opposite vessel Hope approached."}, {"id": "enantios-quote2", "translation": "I will not be ashamed to say the opposite."}, {"id": "enantios-quote3", "translation": "Bringing nothing contrary to this man."}, {"id": "enantios-quote4", "translation": "You have a tongue opposite to Orpheus."}, {"id": "enantios-quote5", "translation": "I would speak knowing well the affairs of the enemy."}, {"id": "enantios-quote6", "translation": "I say to your enemies that you, father, appear as an avenger."}, {"id": "enantios-quote7", "translation": "May you have an inescapable wrestling hold against your enemies."}, {"id": "enantios_adv-orth1", "translation": "contrarily"}, {"id": "enantios_adv-def1", "translation": "contrarily"}, {"id": "enantios_adv-quote1", "translation": "How do you not say these things contrarily to them?"}, {"id": "enarges-orth1", "translation": "clear, evident"}, {"id": "enarges-def1", "translation": "clear, evident"}, {"id": "enarges-quote1", "translation": "A clear report came to Inachus."}, {"id": "enarges-quote2", "translation": "But never yet did I see such a clear dream."}, {"id": "enargos-orth1", "translation": "clearly, manifestly"}, {"id": "enargos-def1", "translation": "clearly, manifestly"}, {"id": "enargos-quote1", "translation": "Guard the city and care for it clearly."}, {"id": "enarizo-orth1", "translation": "to kill"}, {"id": "enarizo-def1", "translation": "to kill"}, {"id": "enarizo-quote1", "translation": "Why did you not kill the man yourself?"}, {"id": "enaroktantas-orth1", "translation": "stripping the slain"}, {"id": "enaroktantas-def1", "translation": "stripping the slain"}, {"id": "enaroktantas-note1", "translation": "Hesychius, ἐναροφόρος [bearing spoils]: σκυλοφόρος [bearing spoils]."}]}